ource":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:bb53ad0686c89026c27f2fd99b66d3b489fb406ccac4eb6b667382a95fd91b18","file":"preprints/Semialgebraic-universal-covers-of-normal-projective-varieties-September-24-2026/build/main.tex","line":92,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"654662dbaca79f33831c0de22cfa50c018f2122fca23e5ace6774721cc54c340","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Semialgebraic-universal-covers-of-normal-projective-varieties-September-24-2026/build/main.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:bb53ad0686c89026c27f2fd99b66d3b489fb406ccac4eb6b667382a95fd91b18","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Semialgebraic-universal-covers-of-normal-projective-varieties-September-24-2026/build/main.tex#L92"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nLet \\(X\\) be a connected normal projective variety over \\(\\C\\), and let\n\\(\\widetilde X\\) be its universal cover. The following conditions are\nequivalent:\n\\begin{enumerate}[label=\\textup{(\\roman*)}]\n\\item \\(\\widetilde X\\) is biholomorphic to a semialgebraic open subset\nof a projective variety.\n\\item There are an integer \\(m\\geq0\\), a bounded symmetric domain \\(D\\),\nand a simply connected normal projective variety \\(F\\) such that\n\\[\n                 \\widetilde X\\simeq D\\times\\C^m\\times F.\n\\]\n\\end{enumerate}\nA point is allowed as either \\(D\\) or \\(F\\). No algebraicity of the\ndeck transformations is assumed."}
